# An eliminated player stays eliminated while the round is still running
#
# The other half of the fix 14 covers. MatchKartsToPlayers is gated on
# is_menu_active() because make_player puts PlayerID on the kart itself, so a
# mid-round rebuild hands an eliminated player a fresh kart with a full stock of
# lives. 14 cannot see it: with one kart, killing it also ends the round, and
# with no gamepad ProvidesMaxGamepadID::count() is 1, so once the last player is
# gone "size() + 1 == count()" is true and the function returns before it could
# rebuild anyone.
#
# Reaching the rebuild needs a player missing while another player is still
# there, and the round still running -- so three karts: two players and a bot.
# Two players is the ceiling; at three, MatchKartsToPlayers' "a player left"
# branch (size() > count() + 1) fires in the menu and deletes the ones with no
# gamepad. Hence the bot for the third contender.
#
# No screenshots: a bot is on the field.

disable_animations

set_round_type Lives
goto_screen Main
wait 0.2

add_player 1
add_ai
wait_frames 3
expect_car_count 3

start_round
wait_frames 3
expect_state Playing

# reset_car_trackers has run by now. The two survivors get spare lives so the
# bot cannot end the round from under the assertion; only the scripted death
# below is meant to count.
set_tracker_at 1 lives 5
set_tracker_at 2 lives 5
expect_tracker_at 0 lives 1

set_tracker_at 0 health 0
wait_frames 10

# Player 0 is gone, the round is still going because two contenders remain,
# and nothing put player 0 back. Without the menu-only guard MatchKartsToPlayers
# rebuilds them here and this is 3.
expect_state Playing
expect_car_count 2
expect_tracker_at 0 lives 5

wait_frames 20
expect_car_count 2

end_round
wait_frames 5
expect_state Menu

# From the menu the rebuild is correct, and is what puts player 0 back for the
# scripts after this one.
remove_ai
wait_frames 3
remove_player 1
wait_frames 5
expect_car_count 1

goto_screen Main
wait 0.2
